// Title: UAC Bypass WSReset
// Sigma ID: 89a9a0e0-f61a-42e5-8957-b1479565a658
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Christian Burkard (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-08-23 | Modified: 2024-12-01
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, T1548.002
// Description: Detects the pattern of UAC Bypass via WSReset usable by default sysmon-config
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Wsreset/
//   - https://github.com/hfiref0x/UACME
//   - https://medium.com/falconforce/falconfriday-detecting-uac-bypasses-0xff16-86c2a9107abf
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_uac_bypass_wsreset_integrity_level.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\wsreset.exe" and (ProcessIntegrityLevel in~ ("High", "System", "S-1-16-16384", "S-1-16-12288"))
